WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.269 --> 00:00:01.930
Are you bored with where you work?

00:00:01.930 --> 00:00:04.830
There’s no shame in it, a lot of people
are.

00:00:04.830 --> 00:00:08.880
Or maybe you hit a run of bad luck recently,
and you got furloughed or let go from your

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:09.880
old job.

00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:14.049
It’s a stressful time, and you’re probably
asking: What type of career would be right

00:00:14.049 --> 00:00:15.180
for me?

00:00:15.180 --> 00:00:20.030
Maybe you want some excitement - like chasing
down escaped monsters from high-security containment

00:00:20.030 --> 00:00:21.280
facilities.

00:00:21.280 --> 00:00:25.900
Maybe you want something a little more intellectually
engaging - like joining some of the world’s

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:30.140
finest minds in finding the answers to mysterious
ancient secrets.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:34.710
Or maybe you’re the ambitious type - Someone
with plenty of hashtag Hustle.

00:00:34.710 --> 00:00:38.960
Perhaps nothing would satisfy you more than
climbing to the very top of the corporate

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:43.510
ladder, into a position that would make you
one of the most powerful human beings on the

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:44.510
planet.

00:00:44.510 --> 00:00:48.790
If any or even all of these sound like they
describe you, then maybe your perfect career

00:00:48.790 --> 00:00:54.489
would be working for The SCP Foundation - an
incredibly powerful, top secret organization

00:00:54.489 --> 00:01:01.310
devoted to securing, containing, and protecting
the supernatural across the globe and beyond.

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:05.659
You could be one of the thousands of little
turning cogs that keeps this organization

00:01:05.659 --> 00:01:09.149
running, and keeps the world safe from supernatural
threats.

00:01:09.149 --> 00:01:12.219
But you can’t even get into your local country
club.

00:01:12.219 --> 00:01:15.560
How can you find your way into one of the
most elite groups in history?

00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:20.380
Well, we can’t pretend it’ll be easy,
but it’s definitely not impossible - today,

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:24.729
we’re going to give you a primer on the
potential ways you could join the proud ranks

00:01:24.729 --> 00:01:27.029
of the SCP Foundation.

00:01:27.029 --> 00:01:31.049
With help from files and evidence across the
Foundation database, we’ve figured out many

00:01:31.049 --> 00:01:36.570
of the different positions available at the
SCP Foundation, and what actions and qualifications

00:01:36.570 --> 00:01:38.890
you may need to make the cut.

00:01:38.890 --> 00:01:43.459
Though we can’t promise you won’t be terminated,
vaporized, eaten, or sent to a terrifying

00:01:43.459 --> 00:01:45.259
pocket dimension in the process.

00:01:45.259 --> 00:01:49.229
First, it’s vital to know exactly what you’re
applying for.

00:01:49.229 --> 00:01:54.060
The SCP Foundation is a complex group, but
thankfully for us, it does have a command

00:01:54.060 --> 00:01:56.909
structure that’s pretty easy to understand.

00:01:56.909 --> 00:02:00.609
This will help us figure out the positions
on offer, so you can update your LinkedIn

00:02:00.609 --> 00:02:01.609
profile accordingly.

00:02:01.609 --> 00:02:06.659
There are two main categories of jobs at play
here: We have Security Clearance Categories,

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:11.330
which range from zero to five, and we have
Personnel Classifications, which run from

00:02:11.330 --> 00:02:13.360
A-Class to E-Class.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:18.330
Let us break it down for you: Level 0 Security
Clearance covers jobs like logistics and janitorial

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:19.330
services.

00:02:19.330 --> 00:02:24.450
They’re the lowest entry level of any Foundation
jobs, and you’ll basically be told nothing.

00:02:24.450 --> 00:02:26.890
You might as well be cleaning the bathrooms
at a local gym.

00:02:26.890 --> 00:02:32.200
Level 1 covers most of the same jobs as Level
0, except these staff members perform their

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:37.250
jobs in closer proximity to anomalies - so
you’ll still be cleaning bathrooms, but

00:02:37.250 --> 00:02:39.520
at greater risk to your life.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:43.790
Level 2 is the most common level of Clearance,
and covers most of the jobs you can apply

00:02:43.790 --> 00:02:45.010
for at the Foundation.

00:02:45.010 --> 00:02:49.070
Junior researchers, field operatives, containment
specialists.

00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:53.260
You have a decent grasp on the strangeness
of your profession, but you’re still locked

00:02:53.260 --> 00:02:55.220
out of the major secrets.

00:02:55.220 --> 00:03:00.541
Level 3 is a step up, and covers most senior
research staff, project managers, security

00:03:00.541 --> 00:03:05.710
officers, response team members, and Mobile
Task Force operatives - all of which we’ll

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:06.930
discuss more later.

00:03:06.930 --> 00:03:12.030
Level 4 is Top Secret, and reserved only for
senior administrative positions, like Site

00:03:12.030 --> 00:03:15.820
Directors, Security Directors, or Mobile Task
Force Commanders.

00:03:15.820 --> 00:03:22.210
Finally, Level 5 - which gives access to every
secret the Foundation holds and more.

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:26.490
This is reserved largely for the O5 Council
and those working directly under them.

00:03:26.490 --> 00:03:30.410
We’re not saying it’s necessarily impossible
for you to get into one of those thirteen

00:03:30.410 --> 00:03:34.210
seats of ultimate power, but it’s probably
impossible.

00:03:34.210 --> 00:03:38.810
The A through E personnel classes are a little
easier to process - the further along your

00:03:38.810 --> 00:03:43.900
letter is in the alphabet, the more dangerous
your job, because you work in closer proximity

00:03:43.900 --> 00:03:45.270
to anomalies.

00:03:45.270 --> 00:03:49.850
A-Class staff are considered critical to the
running of the Foundation, like the O5 Council,

00:03:49.850 --> 00:03:52.990
so they’re usually not even allowed near
an anomaly.

00:03:52.990 --> 00:03:58.040
D-Class, as you probably already know, are
guinea pigs regularly thrown into the clutches

00:03:58.040 --> 00:04:00.770
of anomalies to see what happens.

00:04:00.770 --> 00:04:05.850
The only thing worse is E-Class: Which applies
to agents who are already under the active

00:04:05.850 --> 00:04:09.940
effects of anomalies, and thus, are quarantined.

00:04:09.940 --> 00:04:14.350
Now that you fully understand the command
structure of the SCP Foundation, we can talk

00:04:14.350 --> 00:04:19.220
about specific roles, and what it may take
to find these various job titles attached

00:04:19.220 --> 00:04:20.220
to your name.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:24.509
We’ll start with the lowest of the low,
and work our way up to the top of the pyramid.

00:04:24.509 --> 00:04:27.789
Starting, of course, with D-Class.

00:04:27.789 --> 00:04:31.810
The upside of D-Class is that you don’t
really need any kind of qualifications to

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:36.699
join - the majority of D-Class personnel are
death row inmates, so if you commit a few

00:04:36.699 --> 00:04:41.449
capital offenses and get yourself caught,
you’ll likely be up for consideration.

00:04:41.449 --> 00:04:46.650
After all, employee turnaround for D-Class
is pretty crazy, for obvious reasons.

00:04:46.650 --> 00:04:51.030
The downside is that you really, really, really
don’t want to become a D-Class.

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:56.569
While there are some rare examples of the
lives of D-Classes being improved - like one

00:04:56.569 --> 00:05:02.559
who was released to pursue a law degree after
being educated by SCP-5094 - it’s largely

00:05:02.559 --> 00:05:04.590
a literally dead end job.

00:05:04.590 --> 00:05:08.720
But let’s say you’re a little luckier
than that and the job you seek, while still

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:12.469
dangerous, will at least get you a decent
pension and dental coverage.

00:05:12.469 --> 00:05:17.080
We’re talking about the day to day, bread
and butter jobs that keep the whole Foundation

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:18.370
running: Site Staff.

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:22.940
If you’re working on site at any of the
hundreds or even thousands of secure areas

00:05:22.940 --> 00:05:28.349
the Foundation maintains across the globe,
you have four different possible career paths:

00:05:28.349 --> 00:05:34.020
Containment Specialist, Researcher, Security
Officer, and Tactical Response Officer.

00:05:34.020 --> 00:05:38.419
Containment specialists are, as you can probably
tell from the name, experts in maintaining

00:05:38.419 --> 00:05:40.529
containment for anomalies.

00:05:40.529 --> 00:05:43.650
This career path forks into two possible branches.

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:48.930
In the more active of the two branches, Containment
Specialists enter zones of active, anomalous

00:05:48.930 --> 00:05:54.289
activity, and contain the anomaly for transport
back to the nearest operational site.

00:05:54.289 --> 00:05:58.310
To join this career path, you’d likely be
expected to come from a military background

00:05:58.310 --> 00:06:01.249
due to the risky and tactical nature of the
job.

00:06:01.249 --> 00:06:04.169
The second branch is a little less hands on.

00:06:04.169 --> 00:06:08.740
These are the actual engineers and technicians
who work with researchers to devise the containment

00:06:08.740 --> 00:06:10.990
procedures for the various SCPs.

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:16.470
For this role, you’ll not only need to likely
understand physics and engineering at an expert

00:06:16.470 --> 00:06:20.069
level, you’ll also need an extraordinarily
creative mind.

00:06:20.069 --> 00:06:24.129
You need to think outside the box to keep
the anomalies in the box.

00:06:24.129 --> 00:06:28.490
A recurring theme you’ll find when it comes
to Foundation jobs is that you don’t seek

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:33.699
out the Foundation for a job, if you’re
the right person and show potential, they’ll

00:06:33.699 --> 00:06:35.120
find you.

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:36.919
Researchers are a similar story.

00:06:36.919 --> 00:06:40.949
These are the best research scientists in
the world, scouted by the Foundation to assist

00:06:40.949 --> 00:06:41.990
the cause.

00:06:41.990 --> 00:06:46.050
If you’re someone with a true passion for
science - with topics including, but not limited

00:06:46.050 --> 00:06:51.490
to, biology, physics, chemistry, botany, and
xenobiology - and you’re willing to put

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:56.240
in the work to reach the very top of your
field, the Foundation may just come knocking

00:06:56.240 --> 00:06:57.449
at your door.

00:06:57.449 --> 00:07:02.550
Much like a lot of prestigious universities,
the Foundation also sometimes considers legacy

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:03.550
candidates.

00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:08.059
The famous Dr. Bright, for example, became
a member of the Foundation’s research corps

00:07:08.059 --> 00:07:12.240
because his mother and father worked for the
Foundation, and it didn’t hurt that several

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:14.789
of his siblings were anomalous too.

00:07:14.789 --> 00:07:19.309
Next, Security Officers, more informally known
as Guards.

00:07:19.309 --> 00:07:23.419
This job is worth applying for the paycheck
alone as there’s likely some good hazard

00:07:23.419 --> 00:07:25.020
pay attached to it.

00:07:25.020 --> 00:07:29.619
Most Security Officers perform physical guard
duties and are recruited from law enforcement,

00:07:29.619 --> 00:07:32.050
the corrections industry, and the military.

00:07:32.050 --> 00:07:38.199
However, the other half of the Security Officers
work in information security and, as a result,

00:07:38.199 --> 00:07:42.610
are chosen for their IT prowess and their
backgrounds in the intelligence community.

00:07:42.610 --> 00:07:48.189
And finally, as far as Site Staff are concerned,
we have Tactical Response Officers.

00:07:48.189 --> 00:07:52.970
Don’t expect to get this job if your background
is civilian though since these special operatives

00:07:52.970 --> 00:07:58.330
are the first line of defense between Foundation
sites and external threats, from anomalous

00:07:58.330 --> 00:08:02.250
attackers to hostile groups of interest trying
to infiltrate.

00:08:02.250 --> 00:08:07.379
If you want this job, you really need to put
in the hours, days, months, and years rising

00:08:07.379 --> 00:08:09.389
through the ranks in the military.

00:08:09.389 --> 00:08:13.539
If you do get the job though, you’ll likely
be stationed at one of the larger and more

00:08:13.539 --> 00:08:17.619
important sites to remain on constant guard
for any potential threats.

00:08:17.619 --> 00:08:21.379
But let’s say you don’t want to work on
a containment site.

00:08:21.379 --> 00:08:24.810
Maybe you want to travel, see the world, get
a little excitement.

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:30.039
Thankfully, there are two different career
paths that allow you to do just that - Field

00:08:30.039 --> 00:08:32.630
Agents and Mobile Task Force members.

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:37.050
The Field Agent position is one of the more
accessible in the Foundation, largely because

00:08:37.050 --> 00:08:39.370
of the fact there are so many ways in.

00:08:39.370 --> 00:08:43.670
If you’re an exceptionally observant and
discrete person, this job is probably for

00:08:43.670 --> 00:08:47.290
you seeing as it’s essentially being a spy
for the Foundation.

00:08:47.290 --> 00:08:51.530
You may be offered the job if you work in
law enforcement, the government, or any kind

00:08:51.530 --> 00:08:53.560
of emergency service.

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:58.310
These undercover agents also infiltrate groups
of interest or secret societies the Foundation

00:08:58.310 --> 00:09:03.530
wishes to keep an eye on, like the Serpent’s
Hand or the Children of the Scarlet King.

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:07.730
If you’re in any of these positions, or
already work as a field agent for the mainstream

00:09:07.730 --> 00:09:12.930
intelligence community, becoming a Foundation
Field Agent may be your calling.

00:09:12.930 --> 00:09:16.030
Mobile Task Forces are a little more extreme.

00:09:16.030 --> 00:09:20.670
They’re made up of elite operatives drawn
from all over the Foundation, often with a

00:09:20.670 --> 00:09:23.330
heavy emphasis on military experience.

00:09:23.330 --> 00:09:28.550
The more specialized you are, the more likely
you are to land a spot on one of these teams.

00:09:28.550 --> 00:09:30.430
Are you an expert in explosives?

00:09:30.430 --> 00:09:33.580
Try for MTF Epsilon-9, the "Fire Eaters.”

00:09:33.580 --> 00:09:37.120
Are you an expert in epidemiology and biohazard
containment?

00:09:37.120 --> 00:09:39.560
Join MTF Beta-7, dubbed the "Maz Hatters.”

00:09:39.560 --> 00:09:43.450
Are you a benevolent anomaly aligned with
the interests of the Foundation?

00:09:43.450 --> 00:09:48.050
MTF Alpha-9, aka "Last Hope” is just for
you!

00:09:48.050 --> 00:09:53.890
The Foundation sometimes even recruits ex-members
of enemy groups of interest into MTFs on occasion.

00:09:53.890 --> 00:09:59.070
Of course, despite there being plenty of ways
into this profession, none of them are easy,

00:09:59.070 --> 00:10:04.160
and the job carries huge risks due to how
often MTFs see combat.

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:06.840
What if you’ve always been more of a leader
than a follower though?

00:10:06.840 --> 00:10:11.480
You’re a natural manager, someone who has
all their anomalous ducks in a row.

00:10:11.480 --> 00:10:15.930
Perhaps you’re eyeing the role of Site Director,
the one who all other department heads on

00:10:15.930 --> 00:10:17.900
site report directly to.

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:19.870
How do you get your foot in the door?

00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:20.870
It’s simple.

00:10:20.870 --> 00:10:24.640
Site Directors start off working some other
job for the Foundation, like researcher or

00:10:24.640 --> 00:10:28.700
Security Officer, and simply climb through
the ranks until they reach the most senior

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:30.870
position in the site where they work.

00:10:30.870 --> 00:10:35.490
Oftentimes, Site Directors were previously
very committed researchers, like Dr. Bright

00:10:35.490 --> 00:10:37.110
or Dr. Gears.

00:10:37.110 --> 00:10:42.610
And finally, the biggest question of all:
How does one become a member of the legendary

00:10:42.610 --> 00:10:44.450
O5 Council?

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:50.320
Due to the extremely mysterious nature of
the Council, this one is hard to say.

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:55.680
Exact information about each member and their
past is shrouded in secrecy, but it stands

00:10:55.680 --> 00:11:00.460
to reason that any new members are elected
in by a majority of the pre-existing council

00:11:00.460 --> 00:11:01.930
members on the board.

00:11:01.930 --> 00:11:06.600
Like Dr. Bright’s father, Adam Bright, it
is theoretically possible to work your butt

00:11:06.600 --> 00:11:11.770
off and get onto the O5 Council through decades
of pure grit, but you’re probably wasting

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:12.840
your time.

00:11:12.840 --> 00:11:15.580
The Council works in mysterious ways after
all...

00:11:15.580 --> 00:11:20.050
If we’ve learned anything today, it’s
that any job actually worth having at the

00:11:20.050 --> 00:11:22.930
SCP Foundation isn’t gotten easily.

00:11:22.930 --> 00:11:27.990
But hey, considering the SCP Foundation has
its shadowy fingers in every pie, and its

00:11:27.990 --> 00:11:33.430
thousands of factions worldwide are masked
by just as many public-facing front businesses,

00:11:33.430 --> 00:11:36.950
for all you know, you might be working for
the Foundation already.

00:11:36.950 --> 00:11:43.600
Now go watch “SCP - 5545 - Mysterious Tunnels
In Antarctica - ABNORMALITY” and “SCP

00:11:43.600 --> 00:11:45.030
- 5000 - Why?

00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:50.279
The Full Story Compilation” to unlock more
secrets from the world of the SCP Foundation.

